CORE
main.cpp
--cpp98
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ unwound in reverse: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [except.ctor]/3: when the initialization of member t of S throws,
the already constructed m2 and base B (and its member b) are destroyed in
reverse order.  The front end only unwound local objects, so nothing was
destroyed (bin53).  The converted constructor body now wraps what follows
each subobject initialization in `try { ... } catch(...) { destroy;
throw; }'.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only
its WRONG assertion.
